window.docContents[81].resolve({"/Class-group-checks/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Class-group-checks":{"contents":"\n\nThe Minkowski bound for quadratic fields (Qsqrtd.minkowskiBound). This\nspecializes the number-field Minkowski bound to the quadratic field\n, using\nthe discriminant formula as the size input.\n\nMinkowski representatives of ideal classes\n(exists_ideal_in_class_of_norm_le). Every ideal class has a representative\nwhose norm is at most the specialized Minkowski bound.\n\nThe imaginary quadratic Minkowski bound\n(exists_ideal_in_class_of_norm_le_imaginary). In the imaginary case the\nconstant is , refining\nthe generic representative bound.\n\nThe real quadratic Minkowski bound\n(exists_ideal_in_class_of_norm_le_real). In the real case the constant is\n, again refining\nthe generic representative bound.\n\nBounded representatives in \n(SqrtNeg5.exists_ideal_in_class_of_norm_le). The  example\ncontains concrete bounded-norm checks that exercise\nthe imaginary Minkowski bound and\nthe representative theorem, alongside\nthe concrete ideal factorizations.\n\nNumeric estimates for the imaginary quadratic Minkowski bound\n(minkowskiBound_lt_of_neg). If , then the bound is below\n. The factor  lets every estimate run on the crude inequality\n, which suffices for all nine Heegner discriminants.\n\nClass-group triviality from inert primes\n(classGroup_eq_one_of_forall_le_minkowskiBound_isInertIn). If every rational\nprime below the Minkowski bound is inert in\n, then every ideal class is trivial. The\nproof takes a bounded representative,\nchecks its prime divisors using the inertness hypothesis and\nthe splitting API, and then applies\nthe Dedekind principality criterion.\n\nClass number one from inert primes\n(classNumber_eq_one_of_forall_le_minkowskiBound_isInertIn). This packages\nthe class-group triviality\ncriterion as the numerical class-number statement\n.\n\nFinite norm search for class groups. A future class-group pipeline should\nextend the inert-primes certificate to\nfinite norm searches that also handle split and ramified small primes\n(computing nontrivial class groups, e.g.  from\nthe √-5 checks) and the real\nquadratic branch of the Minkowski bound.\n\n","context":"Quadratic Number Fields Blueprint","header":"8. Class-group checks","id":"/Class-group-checks/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Class-group-checks"}});